Largest N with M(N) <= 40 MB (decimal, 40e6 B): 250,000 (C = 0.9490); <= 40 MiB: 262,144 (C = 0.9503). Headroom basis: 2.613 - 2.557 GB (decimal) = 56 MB.
M(N) assumes dense 20-double vectors; a sparse layout would be smaller but its size depends on the rows' non-zeros (not computed).

Zipf fit: least squares of ln(count) on ln(rank) (rank from 1).

